WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.630
Answering Questions.

2
00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:05.387
Day 5 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.137 --> 00:00:08.161
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:17.849
Today's goal: answer questions clearly and politely: short or full, saying no politely, giving reasons, and saying I'm not sure without sounding weak.

5
00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:20.053
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.253
The answer ladder: choose your length.

7
00:00:23.503 --> 00:00:24.420
Step 1:

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.489
Short:

9
00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:29.204
Yes, it is. fast, casual, enough for simple facts.

10
00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:30.401
Step 2:

11
00:00:30.681 --> 00:00:31.961
Short + detail:

12
00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:35.889
Yes, it's on the second floor. the most useful everyday answer.

13
00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.087
Step 3:

14
00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.668
Answer + reason:

15
00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:43.343
No, I can't come, because I have a client call. for requests and decisions.

16
00:00:43.623 --> 00:00:44.583
Step 4:

17
00:00:44.863 --> 00:00:48.639
Answer + reason + next step: ...but I can join at 5.

18
00:00:48.919 --> 00:00:51.265
Does that work? the most professional answer.

19
00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:53.490
Part 2.

20
00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.562
Answer the question that was asked.

21
00:00:56.812 --> 00:00:58.156
Here is a quick table:

22
00:00:58.436 --> 00:01:01.039
Question, and Unclear answer, and Clear answer.

23
00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:02.535
When will it be ready?

24
00:01:02.815 --> 00:01:03.924
Unclear answer:

25
00:01:04.204 --> 00:01:05.377
We are working on it.

26
00:01:05.657 --> 00:01:06.681
Clear answer:

27
00:01:06.961 --> 00:01:08.220
By Thursday evening.

28
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.759
How much is the room?

29
00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:11.148
Unclear answer:

30
00:01:11.428 --> 00:01:13.007
It's a very good room, sir...

31
00:01:13.287 --> 00:01:14.311
Clear answer:

32
00:01:14.591 --> 00:01:18.153
3,500 rupeesa night, including breakfast.

33
00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:19.457
Where do you live?

34
00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:20.847
Unclear answer:

35
00:01:21.127 --> 00:01:21.788
Near.

36
00:01:22.068 --> 00:01:23.092
Clear answer:

37
00:01:23.372 --> 00:01:25.697
In Indiranagar, near the metro station.

38
00:01:25.977 --> 00:01:27.428
Did you finish the report?

39
00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:28.817
Unclear answer:

40
00:01:29.097 --> 00:01:30.975
Actually I was doing many things...

41
00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:32.279
Clear answer:

42
00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.412
Not yet.

43
00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.335
I'll send it by 4 pm.

44
00:01:36.685 --> 00:01:38.605
Answer first, explain after.

45
00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:40.851
Part 3.

46
00:01:41.131 --> 00:01:42.517
Saying no politely.

47
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.111
Here is a quick table:

48
00:01:45.391 --> 00:01:47.290
Situation, and Polite no.

49
00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:48.274
Offer:

50
00:01:48.554 --> 00:01:50.965
No, thank you. / I'm fine, thanks.

51
00:01:51.245 --> 00:01:52.525
Request you can't do:

52
00:01:52.805 --> 00:01:54.490
I'm sorry, I can't today.

53
00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.007
Could we do it tomorrow?

54
00:01:56.287 --> 00:01:57.269
Invitation:

55
00:01:57.549 --> 00:01:59.383
Thank you so much for inviting me.

56
00:01:59.663 --> 00:02:01.839
Unfortunately, I have plans that day.

57
00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.527
Something not available:

58
00:02:03.807 --> 00:02:05.279
Sorry, we don't have that.

59
00:02:05.559 --> 00:02:06.797
We have this instead.

60
00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:08.101
Disagreeing:

61
00:02:08.381 --> 00:02:09.725
I'm not sure I agree.

62
00:02:10.005 --> 00:02:11.007
Here's why...

63
00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:13.275
Part 4.

64
00:02:13.555 --> 00:02:15.240
When you don't know or aren't sure.

65
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.834
Here is a quick table:

66
00:02:18.114 --> 00:02:19.223
Instead of, and Say.

67
00:02:19.503 --> 00:02:20.442
I don't know.

68
00:02:20.722 --> 00:02:21.597
(and stop):

69
00:02:21.877 --> 00:02:24.309
I'm not sure, but I'll find out and let you know.

70
00:02:24.589 --> 00:02:26.146
A guess presented as fact:

71
00:02:26.426 --> 00:02:28.879
I think it's on Friday, but let me confirm.

72
00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:30.055
Silence:

73
00:02:30.335 --> 00:02:31.338
Good question.

74
00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.962
Let me think for a second.

75
00:02:33.242 --> 00:02:34.671
Pretending you understood:

76
00:02:34.951 --> 00:02:36.594
Sorry, could you say that again?

77
00:02:37.944 --> 00:02:38.904
Part 5.

78
00:02:39.184 --> 00:02:41.531
Answers with numbers, places and time.

79
00:02:42.781 --> 00:02:43.527
Time:

80
00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:49.503
At half past six. / Around 7. / In about twenty minutes. / By Friday.

81
00:02:49.783 --> 00:02:50.551
Place:

82
00:02:50.831 --> 00:02:55.311
On the second floor. / Next to the bank. / Opposite the bus stand.

83
00:02:55.591 --> 00:02:56.530
Frequency:

84
00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:01.226
Every day. / Twice a week. / Once a month. / Hardly ever.

85
00:03:01.506 --> 00:03:02.487
Duration:

86
00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:07.333
For three years. / Since 2021. / About two hours.

87
00:03:08.683 --> 00:03:09.621
Part 6.

88
00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.907
Conversation: the HR call.

89
00:03:13.157 --> 00:03:15.183
Here is how the conversation goes.

90
00:03:15.463 --> 00:03:16.914
Hi, is this Ashish?

91
00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:19.882
I'm calling from Brightsoft about the backend role.

92
00:03:20.162 --> 00:03:21.591
Yes, this is Ashish.

93
00:03:21.871 --> 00:03:23.258
Thanks for calling.

94
00:03:23.538 --> 00:03:25.906
Is now a good time to talk for ten minutes?

95
00:03:26.186 --> 00:03:27.487
Yes, that's fine.

96
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:28.706
Great.

97
00:03:28.986 --> 00:03:31.525
How many years of experience do you have with Java?

98
00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:34.475
The conversation continues.

99
00:03:34.755 --> 00:03:36.141
About nine years.

100
00:03:36.421 --> 00:03:39.835
I've used Java with Spring Boot for most of that time.

101
00:03:40.115 --> 00:03:42.013
And what's your current notice period?

102
00:03:42.293 --> 00:03:45.216
It's sixty days, but it may be negotiable.

103
00:03:45.496 --> 00:03:48.291
Are you open to working from the office three days a week?

104
00:03:48.571 --> 00:03:49.680
Yes, I am.

105
00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.861
The office is about forty minutes from my home.

106
00:03:54.211 --> 00:03:55.811
The conversation continues.

107
00:03:56.091 --> 00:03:57.734
What's your expected salary?

108
00:03:58.014 --> 00:03:59.401
I'm not sure yet.

109
00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:02.177
I'd like to know more about the role first.

110
00:04:02.457 --> 00:04:04.441
Could you share the budgeted range?

111
00:04:04.721 --> 00:04:06.598
Sure, I'll email it to you today.

112
00:04:06.878 --> 00:04:07.817
Thank you.

113
00:04:08.097 --> 00:04:09.611
I'll look out for it.

114
00:04:10.961 --> 00:04:11.900
Part 7.

115
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.097
Practice.

116
00:04:14.347 --> 00:04:14.987
1.

117
00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.123
Give a short + detail answer.

118
00:04:17.403 --> 00:04:19.153
Is there an ATM near here?

119
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:20.137
2.

120
00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:21.611
Do you work from home?

121
00:04:21.891 --> 00:04:22.638
3.

122
00:04:22.918 --> 00:04:24.177
Have you been to Goa?

123
00:04:25.527 --> 00:04:26.444
Success:

124
00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:27.876
Sample answers.

125
00:04:28.156 --> 00:04:30.268
Yes, there's one next to the pharmacy.

126
00:04:30.548 --> 00:04:31.252
2.

127
00:04:31.532 --> 00:04:32.471
Sometimes.

128
00:04:32.751 --> 00:04:35.012
I work from home on Mondays and Fridays.

129
00:04:35.292 --> 00:04:36.316
Yes, I have.

130
00:04:36.596 --> 00:04:38.068
I went there last December.

131
00:04:39.418 --> 00:04:40.122
2.

132
00:04:40.402 --> 00:04:41.597
Say no politely.

133
00:04:41.877 --> 00:04:43.221
Would you like some sweets?

134
00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:44.567
(you're full) 2.

135
00:04:44.847 --> 00:04:46.191
Can you work this Sunday?

136
00:04:46.471 --> 00:04:47.346
(you can't).

137
00:04:48.696 --> 00:04:49.613
Success:

138
00:04:49.893 --> 00:04:51.045
Sample answers.

139
00:04:51.325 --> 00:04:52.371
No, thank you.

140
00:04:52.651 --> 00:04:54.571
They look delicious, but I'm full.

141
00:04:54.851 --> 00:04:55.555
2.

142
00:04:55.835 --> 00:04:57.669
I'm sorry, I can't this Sunday.

143
00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:01.384
I could. work an extra hour on Monday and Tuesday instead.

144
00:05:01.664 --> 00:05:02.603
Would that help?

145
00:05:03.953 --> 00:05:04.699
3.

146
00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:06.323
Rewrite the weak answer.

147
00:05:06.603 --> 00:05:10.465
When will the fix be deployed? then Actually we are trying, maybe soon.

148
00:05:11.815 --> 00:05:12.732
Success:

149
00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.100
Sample answer.

150
00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.809
Today by 6 pm.

151
00:05:16.089 --> 00:05:17.817
We're running the final tests now.

152
00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.042
Part 8.

153
00:05:20.322 --> 00:05:21.367
Speak today.

154
00:05:22.617 --> 00:05:26.457
Answer every question today with answer first, then explanation.

155
00:05:26.737 --> 00:05:30.172
Say no politely once, with a reason and an alternative.

156
00:05:30.452 --> 00:05:33.332
Use I'm not sure, but I'll find out instead of guessing.

157
00:05:34.682 --> 00:05:36.218
That's the end of this lesson.

158
00:05:36.498 --> 00:05:41.149
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

159
00:05:41.429 --> 00:05:47.551
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

